hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1007","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, H. Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, Sufyan told us, H. Bundar told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu'bah, H. Yahya bin Hakim narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, all of them on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Had, on the authority of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray On the wine.” This is the hadith of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman. And Yusuf said: “He is praying over a piece of cloth that he had that was spread out in his mosque, and I was sleeping next to him, so when he prostrated his garment would touch mine. \And I am menstruating\"""""
"1008","From us Ali bin Hajar, from us Ismail, meaning Ibn Aliyah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Umm Salamah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. “He used to pray over the wine.”"
